{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PRE-REVIEW VERIFICATION against the code S1/S2/S4 actually landed on the stack (front-loaded because three plans in this epic have already had a wrong claim about a SIBLING story, and each cost a review cycle).\n\nTWO SCOPE ITEMS ARE ALREADY DONE — this plan overstates its own work:\n\n(1) 'Bedrock-hosted Claude gets a rebar ModelProfile override because its capability flags differ from the direct Anthropic API' — ALREADY SHIPPED by f184 (closed). src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py:38 _is_claude() covers BOTH hosts: isinstance(profile, AnthropicModelProfile) OR bedrock_thinking_variant == 'anthropic', and the _REBAR_OVERRIDES entry withdraws native_structured_output for both. f184 also added the boto3-gated verified-fake test pinning that Bedrock Claude's real profile carries those fields. S3 must NOT re-add this; it should verify it and move on.\n\n(2) 'Prompt caching is wired through BedrockModelSettings ... selected by the prompt_cache_style == \"bedrock\" capability' — the SELECTION is already shipped: capabilities.py:198 cache_settings_for() returns BedrockModelSettings when prompt_cache_style == 'bedrock', and f184 carries a boto3-gated test asserting both cache keys are set. S3 supplies the missing half only: the builder that makes a Bedrock model exist so that branch is reachable in production.\n\nONE GENUINE CONTRADICTION TO RESOLVE BEFORE IMPLEMENTATION — the number of cache keys:\n\nThis plan names THREE (bedrock_cache_instructions, bedrock_cache_tool_definitions, bedrock_cache_messages). f184 shipped TWO (instructions + tool_definitions) and DELIBERATELY omitted messages, because the direct-Anthropic path sets exactly anthropic_cache_instructions + anthropic_cache_tool_definitions and PARITY was the goal — AnthropicModelSettings also has anthropic_cache_messages and rebar does not set it either.\n\nSo enabling bedrock_cache_messages would make Bedrock cache MORE than the Anthropic path, which is not parity but a new caching behaviour with its own cost/TTL profile. Recommendation: keep TWO keys for parity, and if message-level caching is wanted, make it a separate decision with its own measurement rather than smuggling it in as a third key here. Whichever is chosen, this plan and f184's shipped code must AGREE — right now they do not, and the S6 parity bar is measured against exactly this.\n\nALSO CONFIRMED CORRECT in this plan: the [bedrock] extra is genuinely still absent (f184 carries an AC that it added no boto3 dependency), and pydantic_ai.models.bedrock does import botocore at module top, so the missing-extra error path is real. The unit-tests-without-AWS-credentials AC is achievable — capabilities.py already imports BedrockModelSettings INSIDE the bedrock branch precisely so no botocore import happens unless a Bedrock model is in use.\n\nSTALE CITATION WARNING: this plan cites no line numbers, which is good, but note runner.py is now at EXACTLY the 800-LOC hard cap (task 2682) and providers.py is at 289 against the 300-LOC cap that is an ATTESTED criterion of closed story 7468. The bedrock builder will NOT fit in providers.py. It needs its own leaf module (e.g. src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py, mirroring anthropic_model.py) — decide that in the plan rather than leaving the implementer to breach a signed criterion."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785384877725769001,"uuid":"d8476e18-89ae-41aa-89bb-2748c55a38dd"}